; SCENE: BEDROOM

It was a simple mission.
You held your hand axe over the priestess, while ignoring the staff head pressed against your neck. 

ARIA: So, you’re the one they sent.
ARIA: I was hoping it’d be someone more…
ARIA: Mmm…
ARIA: I don’t know. 
ARIA: More knightly! 
MOIRA: …
MOIRA: …I could say the same thing about you.
ARIA: Oh?
MOIRA: I thought you’d be scarier.
ARIA: I’m plenty terrifying, Miss…?
MOIRA: Moira.
ARIA: Miss Moira, then.
ARIA: ~~
ARIA: ~
MOIRA: Hey–! 

You’re kind of stupid. 
The song pierces through you.

; SCENE TRANSITION → THE VOID

The Old World was a vice. This was the universal truth drilled into you. Anything before the Great Upheaval was a cruel history and any attempt to understand it was unnecessary.

FAUST: What do you plan on doing after graduation?
MOIRA: Continuing my work for the Record Keepers. 
MOIRA: Everything I have done has been for the good of the Recollection effort, so it would be useless if I didn’t continue to apply myself in that regard.
FAUST: Yawn…
FAUST: Boring.
FAUST: Sooo boring, Moimoi.
MOIRA: You seem awfully uninterested for someone who is also graduating. 
FAUST: Well, I’ll just go where you go.
FAUST: That’s how it is, agent and officer.
MOIRA: …Faust.

She taps the skin underneath her right eye. You feel the ache at the base of your neck. 
FAUST: Have you heard the rumors? 
MOIRA: Why the sudden change in topic?
FAUST: Because the last one was way too boring.
MOIRA: You were the one who–
FAUST: So, so?
MOIRA: No, I haven’t. 
FAUST: I heard that they’re going to send people on an expedition to the oldest house.
FAUST: Some final clean-up job.
FAUST: What do you know about Aria of the Dead?
MOIRA: The song? 
FAUST: The person.
FAUST: They call her the end of times.
FAUST: It’s a myth that Marmar told me.
FAUST: They say she’s the reason that the Exorcists lost the war, and how the New World came into being.
FAUST: They say she’s still alive, and that this is the final hunt.
FAUST: Or somethin’ like that~
FAUST: Scary, right?
MOIRA: …
MOIRA: Do you think I could sign up?
FAUST: Huh?!
FAUST: No way they’ll let you!
FAUST: You haven’t even finished the program!
MOIRA: I’ve done enough to get to where I am.
FAUST: Tch…
FAUST: Of course I tell you about the living weapon and you immediately decide to go deal with it.
FAUST: Typical Moimoi…
MOIRA: She’s probably–
ARIA: Just as human as you are?
ARIA: That’s such a silly assessment.
ARIA: Hinadear. 
HINA: [][][][][][][]

; SCENE TRANSITION → BEDROOM

It scratches the walls. 
It leaves raw gashes. It leaves blood in its wake. 
Yet, it finds no satisfaction in this. It bares all of its teeth and howls. 

MOIRA: It’s a bit much, don’t you think?
MOIRA: She’s dead.

It sniffs at the air, stumbling around, trying to get its footing. Four paws, claws in the dirt. 
It looks at her. It 
looks 
at her.

MOIRA: Fuck.

The woman pulls back, hand wrapping around the hilt of her axe. She swings forward. It’s a sloppy move. It knows. 

Run. Run faster. It bites and gnashes and snips.

MOIRA: This was supposed to be an easy job.

Faster. Run faster. Or it’ll catch–

